WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:03.940
Hey Crazies.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.260
I don’t know if you’ve ever noticed, but
there’s something weird about the night sky.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.540
There are bright dots everywhere!

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.600
Most of them are very far away and stay pretty
static relative to each other,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.540
which is why, for thousands of years,
we were convinced they formed a solid shell

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.480
around us.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.640
Thankfully, we've learned that space has a lot more depth than that.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.660
But in this narrow band across the sky, you’ll
find the closest dots.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.880
These are super weird because they’re some
of the brightest in the sky

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.780
and, if you watch long enough,
you can see them move against the background.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.360
Those bright wandering dots are the Planets,
which comes from the Ancient Greek:

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.200
“Planetai Asteres” meaning “Wandering
Star.”

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.640
Actually, in Ancient Greek, the noun comes
before the adjective

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.160
so it would be: “Asteres Planetai” or
“Star Wandering.”

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.540
Whatever! It doesn't matter!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.220
The point is, all the planets, the Sun, and
the Moon are in the same part of the sky.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.400
It’s called the ecliptic because it’s
where all the solar and lunar eclipses happen.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.480
That band also happens to pass through 12
star constellations called the zodiac.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.340
Side note!

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.500
Constellations are completely arbitrary groups
of stars

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.300
made up by people thousands of years ago
probably with the help of some psychotropic

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.080
drugs.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.000
Dude, I think it looks like a lion.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.900
Have you been eating the mushrooms again?

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.580
Astrology is a form of magic from 4000 years
ago.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.240
Astronomy is a completely respectable science and science is what we do here.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.140
End of side note!

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.000
So, to understand why all these objects are
along the ecliptic,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.880
we need to think 3-dimensionally.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.520
The orbit of the Earth around the Sun is called
the “Plane of the Ecliptic.”

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.700
How much another orbit is tilted from this
plane is called its inclination.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.360
For the other 7 planets and the moon, those
inclinations are less than 10 degrees.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.340
That means they all orbit in roughly the same
plane.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.140
But why? What's the deal with that?

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.400
Hmm, that's a good question.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.620
This is only going to make sense if we go
back to the beginning.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.020
To the time machine!

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:58.640
5 billion years ago, the solar system was
just a giant cloud of gas and dust.

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:02.520
and gravity has began to pull it in causing it
to collapse.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.260
As the cloud got smaller, the particles of
gas and dust started to bump into each other more often.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.340
Over the course of about 50 million years,
those collisions took their toll.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.720
Most of the random up-and-down motions of
the particles canceled out

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.500
leaving only the overall spin of the cloud.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.150
It’s now what we call an “Accretion Disk,”
which will eventually form the planets,

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.280
over the next few hundred million years.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.620
Back to the lab!

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.480
So that’s it.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.600
Conservation of momentum turns the cloud into
a plane before the planets even form.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:37.080
I have had it with mother [BEEP] planets in
a mother [BEEP] plane!

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.650
Why wasn’t the Sun at the center of that
cloud also a disk?

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.569
The gas and dust got too close too fast.

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:47.790
Remember, turning that cloud into a disk took
millions of years.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:53.120
By that time, 99.8% of the matter in that
cloud had already fallen into the center.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.470
The Sun was already on its way to forming
long before it had a chance to flatten out.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:02.330
If matter is very loosely packed, then
one piece can travel a long way before it

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:03.599
runs into another piece.

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:05.610
That’s what it looks like in the accretion
disk.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:09.629
However, if matter is tightly packed and held
in place by gravity, then

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:11.760
the pieces can’t get away from the collisions.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.720
They’re stuck.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.920
But that doesn’t mean they don’t try
and that causes a net outward pressure in all directions,

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.400
which forms a sphere, not a disk.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.610
But isn't it still trying to flatten out a little bit?

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.520
Right, so, like with most things, it's a spectrum.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.740
There are two factors at work at the same
time.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.239
Outward pressure from the collisions and angular
momentum from the spin.

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:35.239
If the matter is loose, angular momentum dominates
and you get a disk.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.860
If the matter is dense, outward pressure dominates
and you get a sphere.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:43.240
The angular momentum is always there though,
so even the Earth and the Sun bulge at their

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.520
their equator a little bit.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.580
Most asteroids and comets tend to be sort
of in the awkward in-between.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:53.060
Too dense to be a disk, but too light to be
a sphere, so they turned out lumpy.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.390
So, what’s the weirdest thing you’ve seen
in the sky?

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:56.740
Please share in the comments.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:58.440
Thanks for liking and sharing this video.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.410
Please subscribe if you’d like
to keep up with us.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.960
And until next time, remember, it’s OK to
be a little crazy.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.680
In the last video, we learned how planes fly.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:10.930
Comment response time!
hisham borgol and FiVorT98 were both wondering

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.840
how planes actually move forward.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:13.760
Good question!

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.520
Airplanes have very powerful engines that
turn big turbines or propellers.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.540
The blades of those engines pull the air backward
so hard

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.180
that the plane responds by moving forward.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.820
Also, conservation of momentum.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:31.600
rotflmaopmpqxyz suggested that maybe Newton’s
third law is a better explanation.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.660
Well, yes, Newton’s third law is a valid
explanation if you’re careful,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.100
but I wouldn’t say it’s “better” per
say.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.080
I‘d say it’s about the same for the plane.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.880
Technically, you can get conservation of momentum
from Newton’s third law,

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.860
but you can also get Newton’s third law
from conservation of momentum.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.180
There is nothing that claim either one is
more fundamental than the other.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.000
It just comes down to how your brain works
and what you’re used to.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:56.260
When you do advanced physics a lot like I
do

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.720
Things like Einstein’s relativity and quantum
physics

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.710
you find that Newton’s laws aren’t nearly as useful
as conservation laws,

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.780
so I’m just in the habit of thinking in
terms of conservation laws.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.260
Plus, I think they’re a little more elegant
for deeper understanding.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:13.060
Rogue Assassin Gaming is mind-blown by me
saying air is a fluid.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.620
Yes, air is a fluid.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.400
In fact, any substance that is capable of
flowing is called a fluid.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.340
Basically, any substance whose molecules can
move about freely.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:26.540
That includes both liquids and gases.
and, if you think about it, air and water

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.360
behave in a lot of the same ways.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.600
Water is just so dense you can see it.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.440
That’s all.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.700
Joel Craig wants to know how to use science
to take over the world.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.760
I’ll never reveal my secrets!

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.980
